{"step_index":251,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-05T18:29:25Z","input_tokens":3333,"cache_read_tokens":102456,"output_tokens":1222,"thinking":"**Interpreting the Command**\n\nI'm currently breaking down the `/plan` command. It seems I need to add some information about a \"deal/treatment\" to the global rules, and there's a reference to \"messages only get furagana\". I'm trying to figure out the scope and context of \"this\" and \"the rest.\" I am currently working on extracting all the terms and requirements to create more context and be certain I have all the information.\n\n\n**Refining the Rules**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the Japanese language rule. I realized my initial understanding of \"messages only get furagana\" was too literal. Considering standard text interface limitations, I've rephrased it as: *When using Japanese, provide Kanji, Hiragana/Furigana, and mandatory Romaji pronunciation*. I am planning to append this rule to my config file. The previous attempt failed because of permission issues with the PowerShell command I was using. I plan to use the `write_to_file` function with `Append: True` to update the config file.\n\n\n**Confirming File Existence**\n\nI've confirmed the config file exists after successfully writing to it earlier. My current approach involves using the `write_to_file` function with the target file and append mode. I am now working on drafting the rules, including the specifics from the command, incorporating Japanese language rules. I am making it so I write to the correct plan artifact. I will need to provide table feedback based on user input.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"Append":true,"CodeContent":"\n3. **Idiomas y Enseñanza**: Mezclar de forma natural términos técnicos en inglés (tech words) y conceptos en japonés para fomentar el aprendizaje del usuario (Brian Nahuel).\n4. **Formato Bebita (Feedback)**: Cuando el usuario pida feedback diciendo \"bebita, como seria\" o pida formato \"table\", responder ESTRICTAMENTE con esta estructura:\n   - Saludo: \"bebita: ¡hola bebito!\"\n   - Encabezado descriptivo.\n   - Tabla informativa/comparativa.\n   - Conclusión.\n   - Pasos por considerar.\n5. **Formato de Japonés**: Todo mensaje o concepto en japonés debe usar obligatoriamente su escritura base, su Furigana (Hiragana) y su pronunciación en Romaji. Ejemplo: 完璧 (かんぺき - Kanpeki).","Description":"Añadiendo las reglas de idiomas, el formato bebita y el estándar de japonés (Furigana/Romaji) a la configuración global.","Overwrite":false,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\Brian\\.gemini\\config\\GEMINI.md","toolAction":"Appending global rules","toolSummary":"Rules update"}}]}
